The first thing I remember is the smell of the barn. [[slnc 2500]] It was cold that morning, and my father had already been out there for an hour. [[slnc 3500]] I think I was five or six. [[slnc 1500]] He let me hold the bucket while he milked the cow, and I spilled half of it on my boots. [[slnc 4000]] He did not get angry. He just laughed and said that the cats would be happy. [[slnc 2000]] I have thought about that laugh a lot since he passed. [[slnc 3000]] Some days it is the only thing I can hear clearly.
